# `yo fix --migrate deref` reads source written before the deref rule, where a
# capture-list entry `{ r }` of a reference binding copied the referent and a
# bare `r` at an unbound type binder (`first(r)`) bound the referent's type.
# Since #1891 (R-CAP-1) and R1 the rule reads both as the reference, and the
# recorder read them that way too: the closure became a borrowing one (E0909
# into the sink parameter, the file did not evaluate) and the binder silently
# bound `T := &i32`. The migration now writes `{ r : r.* }` and `first(r.*)`,
# and the migrated file checks
# (issues/fixed/2026-11-13-migrate-deref-reads-a-capture-pun-and-a-binder-read-the-new-way.md).
stdout_keep=^(fix:|error|check:.*(OK|passed|failed))
timeout=240
